 "text": {
  "fr": {
   "name": "3-D Tic-Tac-Toe",
   "genre": "Stratégie",
   "synopsis": "3-D Tic-Tac-Toe pour Atari VCS 2600 est un jeu de société développé par Atari. Le principe du jeu est le même que le Tic-Tac-Toe sur papier, la seule différence étant que l'on peut également faire des alignements en profondeur. Le nombre de X ou O à aligner est de 4.",
   "synopsis_lang": "fr"
  },
  "en": {
   "name": "3-D Tic-Tac-Toe",
   "genre": "Strategy",
   "synopsis": "The game is similar to the traditional game of tic-tac-toe, but is played on four 4x4 grids stacked vertically; it is basically a computerized version of the board game Qubic using traditional tic-tac-toe notation and layout. To win, a player must place four of their symbols on four squares that line up vertically, horizontally, or diagonally, on a single grid, or spaced evenly over all four grids. This creates a total of 76 possible ways to win, in comparison to eight possible ways to win on a standard 3Ã—3 board. The game has nine variations: it can be played by two players against each other, or one player can play against a built-in AI on one of eight different difficulty settings. The game uses the standard joystick controller.",
   "synopsis_lang": "en"
  }
 },
